{
  "_readme": "Audio files for the app (docs/design.md#audio-files). Paths are relative to static/audio/. Add a file and its entry here; no code change. sfx.<id> = a file for a sound id in src/lib/sound/ids.ts (without one, the id plays its procedural placeholder from src/lib/sound/synth.ts): AAC .m4a, mono 44.1 kHz ~64 kbps, under 3 s. music.<sunny|rain|snow>.<00-23> = the Tokyo hour's track, { file, start, end?, gain? }: one seamless loop period (start = the second where the loop begins musically; playback starts there), plus a 3 s copy of the period's start when `end` (where the period ends) is given, for the engine's deck hand-off; without `end` the file is just the period and `<audio loop>` wraps it. gain = dB to the common loudness (-16 LUFS). Written by `npm run audio:music -- <dir>` (scripts/music.ts) from the user's own files: AAC-LC stereo 64 kbps; `npm run audio:music -- --gains` re-measures only the gains. opening = the opening theme (one-shot), { file, start: 0, gain } or a bare path. ambient.<waves|birds|cicadas|higurashi|crickets|wind|rain> = mono loops of 10-30 s. The music files are user-provided and committed by the user's decision (docs/design.md#audio-files). Do not commit downloaded effects.",
